course: dictionary
lesson: 5866
title: Manatees: sea cows, not fish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A manatee is a large, slow, gentle animal that eats plants and lives in warm coastal waters and rivers. Its flippers and round, paddle-shaped tail help it swim. The context helps you here: «Dugongs are sea cows that graze on sea grass» tells you that sea cows eat plants.
explain: A manatee is called a sea cow, but it is not a cow. The word is a clue: a cow is a slow, gentle animal that eats plants, and a manatee is too. «Steller's sea cow was a giant, gentle cousin of the manatee» shows that the two animals are related.
explain: Look for clues about what kind of animal it is. A manatee lives in water, but it is a mammal, not a fish. It breathes air and feeds its babies milk, just as a cow or a cat does. So when you read about manatees, ask: do they breathe air, or do they breathe through gills?
fact: A manatee is a large, slow, gentle plant-eater.
fact: A manatee is a mammal: it breathes air and feeds its babies milk.
fact: Manatees live in warm coastal waters and rivers, such as Florida, the Caribbean, West Africa and the Amazon.
fact: «Manatee zones» are places where boats must go slowly, because boat propellers often injure manatees.
fact: Sailors long ago may have mistaken manatees for mermaids.
exercise: «Dugongs are sea cows that graze on sea grass.» What does this tell you about sea cows? | They are very fast swimmers | They live only on dry land | *They eat plants | They hunt other fish
exercise: Which clue shows that a manatee is a mammal and not a fish? | It lives in coastal waters | It is called a sea cow | *It feeds its babies milk | It has flippers
exercise: Why are there «manatee zones» where boats must go slowly? | *Boat propellers often injure manatees | Boats are not allowed to float there | Manatees like to race boats | Manatees are too small to see
test: Which words best describe a manatee? | Hard-shelled and still | Fast and noisy | Tiny and fierce | *Large, slow and gentle
test: Why might sailors long ago have thought manatees were mermaids? | Manatees sing loudly on the shore | Manatees wear jewellery | Manatees live in deserts | *Manatees can look like people from a distance in the water
exam: Which statement about manatees is true? | They are fish that breathe through gills | *They are mammals that breathe air and feed their babies milk | They breathe air and feed their babies milk | They eat meat and hunt sharks
